  "question": {
    "text": "If $b$ is the first term of an infinite G. P whose sum is five, then $b$ lies in the interval."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$(-\\infty,-10)$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n $(10, \\infty)$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n $(0,10)$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$(-10,0)$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "First term $=b$ and common ratio $=\\mathrm{r}$\nFor infinite series, Sum $=\\frac{b}{1-r}=5$ $\\Rightarrow b=5(1-\\mathrm{r})$\nSo, interval of $b=(0,10)$ as, $-1 < \\mathrm{r} < 1$ for infinite GP."
  }
}